        question: "How does the geotechnical report shape the Bakersfield review?",
        answer: "The geotechnical report sets the terms for everything below grade and much of the lateral design. The PE checks the foundation design against the report's boring logs and recommendations — bearing values, settlement expectations, expansive-soil or liquefaction notes where they apply — and verifies the seismic site class used in the lateral analysis matches the report. Kern County sites vary: alluvial soils, agricultural land with variable fill, and areas where groundwater or soil chemistry affects foundation choices. I read the report before I read the drawings, because the foundation review is really a check of whether the design believed the report. A foundation the report doesn't support doesn't get sealed.",
